 - `AgentBackend::launch` starts an agent session from an `AgentLaunch`.
 - `AgentBackend::send` sends a prompt to an existing agent session.
+- `AgentBackend::execute_command` runs a selected-agent backend command such as `/status` without
+  treating the command as an ordinary user prompt.
 - `AgentBackend::launch_streaming` and `AgentBackend::send_streaming` provide real-time output to a
   sink of `AgentStreamEvent` values. Their default implementations call the non-streaming methods.
+- `AgentBackend::execute_command_streaming` provides real-time output for selected-agent backend
+  commands. Its default implementation calls `execute_command`.
 - `AgentBackend::shutdown_handle` returns an `AgentShutdownHandle` for terminating active provider
   processes.
 - `AgentStreamEvent` carries status text, streamed agent messages, and streamed errors.
@@ -110,11 +114,12 @@ kill to remaining processes. This behavior is used by provider implementations t
 processes.
 
 New agent providers implement `AgentBackend`; they do not add provider logic to `src/codex.rs`.
-Providers that need real-time UI output should override the streaming methods. Providers implemented
-inside this crate can use the crate-private process registration helpers for shared shutdown.
-Providers outside this crate can implement launch, send, and streaming through the public trait; a
-public lifecycle extension is required before external child processes can participate in the shared
-`AgentShutdownHandle` registry.
+Providers that support interactive backend slash commands override `execute_command`, and providers
+that need real-time UI output should override the streaming methods. Providers implemented inside
+this crate can use the crate-private process registration helpers for shared shutdown. Providers
+outside this crate can implement launch, send, selected-agent commands, and streaming through the
+public trait; a public lifecycle extension is required before external child processes can
+participate in the shared `AgentShutdownHandle` registry.
 
 ## Codex Provider
 
@@ -127,6 +132,9 @@ public lifecycle extension is required before external child processes can parti
   `codex exec` and `codex exec resume` calls. Launch invocations include the injected
   `PromptPolicy`; resumed invocations for known sessions pass only the follow-up message because the
   Codex thread already contains the launch-time policy and repository instructions.
+- `CodexBackend::build_command_invocation` constructs known-session `codex exec resume` calls for
+  selected-agent backend slash commands. The command is passed as the final resume argument and the
+  invocation stdin is empty, so commands such as `/status` are not wrapped as normal prompt text.
 - `CodexBackend::record_launch_reply`, `record_launch_output`, and `session` maintain in-memory
   session state.
 - `CodexBackend` parses Codex `--json` event lines from stdout to capture `thread.started`
@@ -164,6 +172,11 @@ The primary public methods are:
   `send_to_agent_streaming_with_ids` for UI-driven message flows.
 - `CommandChat::shutdown_agents` and `shutdown_handle` for lifecycle cleanup.
 
+`CommandChat::send_to_agent_streaming_with_ids` detects selected-agent messages whose trimmed text
+starts with `/` followed by a non-whitespace character through `selected_agent_backend_command`.
+Those messages call `AgentBackend::execute_command_streaming`; all other selected-agent messages use
+the normal `send_streaming` path and then pass agent output through orchestrator directive handling.
+
 `CommandChat` uses the active `AgentProfile` when launching user agents, reviewers, and linearizers.
 Workflow code must not hard-code `AgentKind::Codex` when the active profile supplies the provider.
 
